# DEPLOY KIT (do not run against prod)

Offline operator kit for the king-x2 / sqrt-Fisher cutover. This directory is
an artifact to review and copy deliberately; building it does not deploy it.
It contains no credentials. Do not run `autodeploy` against production from
this checkout.

## Files and pins

- `expect.json`: old/new commit, code digest, params, gate and Generator paths.
- `old-params.json`, `new-params.json`: the complete old live parameter set and
  the same set with only `null_samples_per_task=2`,
  `irt_draw_rule="sqrt_fisher"`, and the new `recipe.code_digest`.
- `kx2_operator.py`: checkout, journal inspection, public checks and rollback.
  Invoke it as `python3 -I /root/sn120-run/kingx2-deploy/kx2_operator.py COMMAND`.
  Isolated mode avoids stdlib `operator` shadowing and ambient `PYTHONPATH`.
  Parameter changes call the existing `python -I -m sn120_v2 set-params` CLI;
  the journal is never edited directly and no git/R2 fetch is performed.
  Post-checkout apply runs in a fresh interpreter so the old Params schema is
  not retained.
- `autodeploy`: one-shot gate, apply, health and rollback orchestration.
- `dry-run`: isolated synthetic rehearsal using copied journal/public objects,
  an exact committed branch/kit, an external reserve and a real disposable
  ingestd. It starts no production service, run loop, R2/chain operation or GPU
  worker and reads no secrets.
- `QUALIFICATION.md`: offline evidence and limitations.

The final implementation is `c525286580c84d795b3ca7cbdf2302e96fce31ba`, whose
parent is the deployed `d368b2601f06458349cfe3e84adfbf691994fcb3`. The kit-only
commits select that implementation without changing GPU code or params.
`new_digest` independently pins the GPU code. Do not change the pinned SHA,
fetch an unreviewed ref, or arm an altered kit. The implementation commit must
already exist in the target repository.

Copy the reviewed kit outside the live checkout (normally
`/root/sn120-run/kingx2-deploy`). Create `go` only after final review.
`PENDING_IMPLEMENTATION_COMMIT` is refused.

## Generator feed and competing deployments

The old production baseline includes the live Generator consumer, ingestd and
external reserve. This kit does **not** deploy genfeed again, stop/restart
ingestd, seed/reseed/move/hash-copy the live reserve, or clear the inbox.
Checkout changes code only.

`preflight` and `apply` require:

- `reserve-live.path` to contain exactly the expected absolute
  `/root/sn120-run/reserve-live` path;
- that existing reserve to pass read-only verification under its shared ingest
  lock, with no preparation or mutation;
- the existing generator inbox and prior index to exist; and
- `ingestd.pid` to name a live, non-zombie `generator-ingestd.sh` from the
  selected checkout, using the expected prior index.

The daemon PID, full command and `/proc` start ticks are captured before apply.
The fresh new-code child verifies that exact identity after checkout; rollback
verifies it again after old params/code are restored. No stop is needed, so
there is deliberately no ingestd restart path. `start-ingestd` is a preservation
check, not a launch command. A missing, changed or unexpected daemon fails
closed; it is never silently replaced.

The early `deployment-guard` scans `/proc` for genfeed `autodeploy.sh` or
`ol_operator.py`, another king-x2 `autodeploy`, or another king-x2 operator
outside its own ancestry. `autodeploy` runs it before any stop request and
again at the gate immediately before stopping the old loop. A competing
deployment therefore cannot be ignored until after the loop has been stopped.
Dry-run exercises a real competing genfeed-named process and verifies no
stop/code/params mutation.

## Gate, apply and health

`GATE_WANT` defaults to `r000086` from `expect.json`. The documented interface
is:

```
GATE_WANT=r000086 bash /root/sn120-run/kingx2-deploy/autodeploy
```

This is not authorization to execute it. The operator must independently
confirm the current old HEAD, round, journal, loop, Generator state and watchdog
before creating `go`. The kit defaults are production paths, but this build and
its rehearsals use only isolated scratch paths.

`autodeploy` waits for `go`; `disarm` before apply cancels without changing code
or params. After arming it:

1. Refuses competing deployments, an already-disarmed watchdog, a missing run
   log, a passed gate, the wrong old HEAD, an existing stop request, or other
   than exactly one loop.
2. Rechecks the competing-deploy guard at the gate, touches
   `run-loop.stop-after-round`, waits for the old loop to end, and verifies a
   clean authenticated r000086 close (`null`/`applied`, positive `n_tasks`, no
   lease failure since open and no later open).
3. Disarms the watchdog, checks out the implementation and applies the complete
   new params. It verifies code/pinned digests, two king samples, sqrt-Fisher,
   2,000 tasks, 10,000 active tasks and unchanged genfeed `batch_cap=6`, plus
   the exact pre-apply ingestd identity and external reserve.
4. Starts exactly one new-code loop. r000087 must carry the new params, active
   rotation and sqrt-Fisher IRT snapshot. The public named rotation is checked
   against the journal's `state_sha`, size and rotation block; active bytes,
   snapshot identity and the close-produced round report are also checked.
   Public 404/5xx/timeout responses use bounded polling (default 20 minutes).
   `pool/state` remains a private object-store artifact and is never required
   from the public site.
5. Requires the same loop to close r000087 and open r000088. The close must be
   `null`/`applied`, use the new params and 2,000 tasks, have no lease failure,
   and contain exactly two 2,000-character king null strings for every leased
   box. Positive evaluation wall time and local eval phase timing are logged
   with configured limits before `PASS:`.

The stop request is removed on PASS or verified recovery. The watchdog is
re-armed only after PASS or verified old-code recovery. A stuck loop, failed
rollback or failed restart is reported, not hidden as recovery.

## Evidence-preserving rollback

A failure after apply requests stop-after-round, then invokes the supported
`end-round` command only for an open, **undecided** round with no stored result.
The read-only precheck checks every lease's exact sealed-result key, including
failed leases, and is bounded. `end-round` exit 3 remains a second guard against
races or mirror differences. A sealed result is never deleted to force
rollback; an already decided round must be finished normally by `run`. In these
blocked cases the journal, evidence and new code/params remain and no false
old-loop recovery is claimed.

When recovery is permitted, rollback restores **old params first and old code
second**, verifies both old hashes and genfeed `batch_cap=6`, checks the
external reserve and original ingestd identity, starts one old-code loop and
re-arms the watchdog. Params-first is necessary because old code rejects the
new fields. SIGKILL, OOM, power loss and host failure can still require the
operator's independent recovery procedure.

The hourly weight writer, UID mapping, transaction cursor, burn behavior,
chain and training/optimizer lineage are not touched by this kit.

## Isolated rehearsal

From a clean committed kit:

```
D=/home/bb/scratch/kingx2-r086-genfeed/final-normal bash v2/tools/kingx2-deploy/dry-run
KINGX2_DRY_ABORT_AFTER_OPEN=1 D=/home/bb/scratch/kingx2-r086-genfeed/final-abort bash v2/tools/kingx2-deploy/dry-run
```

`D` must be a fresh directory under `/home/bb/scratch`. The harness refuses a
dirty source kit, clones the exact branch head, checks out old `d368b260`, and
copies the kit from the committed branch archive. All eight files must compare
byte-for-byte with the source. Controller writes go to a full private object
store, while operator fetches use a separate production-like public projection:
it excludes `pool/state` and other artifact families the static site does not
serve. `new_commit` remains the pinned implementation;
only the copied public retry window is shortened for the fixture. The old
r000082-open journal advances through synthetic old-code closes to the r000086
gate. The real copied `autodeploy` drives the remainder.

The external reserve is a separate valid prefix, not a packaged-reserve backup.
A real disposable `generator-ingestd.sh` is launched with genfeed's
`setsid nohup bash` construction and an empty local inbox. Static selector,
prior-index, generator-state, inbox, lock/log and reserve files are fingerprinted
without treating normal future ingest appends as deploy mutations. The initial
read-only shared-lock check creates the normal empty `.ingest.lock`; the fixture
then fingerprints it along with every reserve file and requires all bytes to
survive apply and rollback. The PID and proc start ticks must remain identical
through apply and rollback. Only that
verified disposable process is terminated by fixture cleanup.

Normal rehearsal covers competing-deploy refusal, gate/apply, r000087 health,
r000088 open, public active-byte tamper refusal, sealed-result preservation,
separate undecided params-first rollback and the decided-round guard. The
abort-after-open scenario requires an expected nonzero autodeploy result,
undecided no-decision close, old params/code, one old loop, watchdog re-arm and
Generator/ingestd preservation. `KINGX2_DRY_STORE_RESULT_AFTER_OPEN=1` instead
requires rollback refusal and a disarmed watchdog;
`KINGX2_DRY_FAILED_LEASE=1` additionally exercises a failed lease's sealed
result.

All outcomes/LoRAs are synthetic. No production health, GPU throughput, chain,
R2 or live service behavior is claimed. Useful read-only reports (with isolated
paths exported) are `journal-close RID`, `open-check RID`, `public-check RID`,
`health RID`, `generator-check` and `facts`. Live `preflight`, `apply`,
`rollback`, and `start-loop` are operator actions, not inspection commands.
